<div class="encadre">
    <span class="etiquette">What to remember</span>
    <p>
        Gregorian chant is a <strong>plainchant</strong> unified in the Carolingian period,
        with eastern roots, wrongly attributed to Gregory the Great. It was first written
        down in <strong>neumes</strong> (an aide-mémoire for the gesture, 9<sup>th</sup>
        c.), then made precise thanks to <strong>square notation</strong> on a staff
        (11<sup>th</sup> c.). Today several schools bring it back to life. You now have the
        whole context&nbsp;: let us move on to reading the signs themselves.
    </p>
</div>

